      "problem": "Find the first four non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\frac{1}{1-2{x}^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\frac{1}{1-x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & =1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $2{x}^{2}$ in the above expansion and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-2{x}^{2}} & =1+(2{x}^{2})+{(2{x}^{2})}^{2}+{(2{x}^{2})}^{3}+⋯ \\\\  & =1+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{6}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
